#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# e

#% text
# `e` is the constant `e = 2.71828...`, the base of the natural logarithm.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `e` is exact and known to be a positive real; `e^x` is the same as `exp(x)`. `n(e, d)` gives `d` digits.

#% item
# `log(e)` is 1.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
e
#% output
#= e

#% cell
n(e, 40)
#% output
#= 2.7182818284590452353602874713526624977572471

#% cell
log(e)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
e^(im*pi)
#% output
#= -1

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Powers of `e` are exponentials:

#% cell
e^2 == exp(2)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
d(e^x, x)
#% output
#= exp(x)

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The limit definition:

#% cell
limit((1 + 1/k)^k, k -> inf)
#% output
#= e

#% text
# The series:

#% cell
n(sum(1/factorial(k), [k, 0, 20]) - e)
#% output
#= -2.0502980686246613e-20

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `exp`, `log`, `pi`, `euler_gamma`
